  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Bell Boeing Joint Project Office recorded $1.3B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Bell Boeing Joint Project Office received 1,075 awards so far this fiscal year. Bell Boeing Joint Project Office shows an average award size of $1.2M, and obligations are down 0.9% year over year. Bell Boeing Joint Project Office obligations peaked at $2.5B in FY21, then moved to $1.9B in FY22, $947M in FY23, $871M in FY24, and $1.4B in FY25. Bell Boeing Joint Project Office receives the bulk of current-year obligations from the Department of Defense, which obligated $1.3B. Bell Boeing Joint Project Office also received obligations from the General Services Administration totaling $2.1M. Bell Boeing Joint Project Office sells primarily in aircraft-related markets: Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing accounted for $798M, and Aircraft Manufacturing accounted for $498M. Bell Boeing Joint Project Office also sold Computer Systems Design Services for $35.2M and smaller amounts in other NAICS lines, including Engineering Services at $2.1M and Blank Magnetic and Optical Recording Media Manufacturing at $3.1K.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have Bell Boeing Joint Project Office obligations trended over the past fiscal years?",
        "body": "Bell Boeing Joint Project Office obligations were $2.5B in FY21 and $1.9B in FY22. Bell Boeing Joint Project Office obligations fell to $947M in FY23 and $871M in FY24, then rose to $1.4B in FY25 and are $1.3B in FY26 to date. Bell Boeing Joint Project Office obligations are down 0.9% year over year for the current fiscal-year-to-date period."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main federal buyers and what markets does Bell Boeing Joint Project Office serve?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.3B to Bell Boeing Joint Project Office in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $2.1M. Aircraft-related NAICS dominate Bell Boeing Joint Project Office business, with Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $798M and Aircraft Manufacturing at $498M, plus Computer Systems Design Services at $35.2M and smaller markets totaling the remaining obligations."
      }
    ]
